    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/faculty-pro-vice-chancellor-business-and-law--9471-manchester-all-saints-campus/9370/description/": {
      "title": "Faculty Pro-Vice-Chancellor Business and Law",
      "description": "Faculty Pro-Vice-Chancellor Business and Law  - (9471) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Faculty Pro-Vice-Chancellor Business and Law  (9471) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Faculty Pro-Vice-Chancellor Business and Law  - (9471) Manchester Metropolitan University is ambitious, values‑driven and forward‑looking. Recently named Times and Sunday Times Modern University of the Year 2026 and recognised nationally for student satisfaction, outstanding research strengths, sustainability and colleague experience, the University is making significant investments in its people, estate and research capacity as part of its Building on our Success: The Road to 2035 Strategy. The University is now seeking an exceptional academic leader to become its next Faculty Pro‑Vice‑Chancellor for Business and Law. This is a significant appointment at a pivotal moment in Manchester Met's development, offering the opportunity to lead a vibrant, diverse and highly successful Faculty while contributing to institutional leadership as a member of the University Executive Group. The Faculty of Business and Law brings together the internationally recognised Manchester Law School, a triple-accredited Business School ranked among the top 1% globally, and the Centre for Enterprise, which works with businesses, policymakers and partners across the country to drive innovation and support sustainable economic growth. Educating more than 10,000 students each year, the Faculty combines consistently strong student outcomes with research that addresses significant challenges facing business, law and society. Through close partnerships with employers, professional bodies, policymakers and civic organisations, it makes an important contribution to economic growth, innovation and social progress. As Faculty Pro‑Vice‑Chancellor, you will provide visible and inclusive leadership, setting a clear direction and creating an environment in which colleagues and students can thrive. You will work closely with senior leaders across the University to implement strategy, strengthen reputation, performance and impact, and grow the Faculty's national and international profile, including its contribution to the generation, dissemination and translation of knowledge. To achieve this, we are seeking an experienced and inspirational academic leader with a strong international academic profile, a deep understanding of the higher education landscape, and a genuine commitment to people‑led leadership. You will bring strategic vision, operational excellence and energy, with the ability to lead complex academic communities, build meaningful partnerships and deliver excellent education and excellent research with impact. We are committed to equity, diversity and inclusion and warmly encourage applications from candidates from underrepresented groups. Further information *Please do not apply for this vacancy via the university website* Further information, including a detailed candidate pack, along with instructions on how to apply, can be found through our executive recruitment advisors (Odgers), via this link - www.odgers.com/96167 - Closing date: 5pm on Friday 16 October 2026 - Interview date: Tuesday 8 December 2026 in Manchester Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy . #LI-CF1 Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: Business & Law Closing Date: 16 October 2026 Contract Type: Permanent Contracted Hours per week: 37 Benefits 35 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays Travel loan Private medical care (BUPA) Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Meet the recruiter Carlos Favario ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved. Cookie Preferences This site uses cookies and other tracking technologies to improve your browsing experience, show personalised content/ads and analyse site traffic. Select cookies to accept Required cookies These cookies are used to ensure the user has a secure journey through the site. earcusessionid - Used to maintain your session. earcusession - Used to secure your session. earcucc - Used to manage your cookie preferences. Analytics Cookies Analytics cookies or performance cookies are used to track website visitors and their user behaviour. _ga - Used by Google Analytics. _gid - Used by Google Analytics. _gat - Used by Google Analytics. _fbp - Used by Meta (Facebook) Pixel. Accept Cookies Accept All Cookies Customise Cookies Reject All Optional"
