    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/personal-assistant--9365-manchester-all-saints-campus/9273/description/": {
      "title": "Personal Assistant -",
      "description": "Personal Assistant  - (9365) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Personal Assistant  (9365) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Personal Assistant  - (9365) About the Role An exciting opportunity has arisen for a highly organised, proactive, and professional Personal Assistant (PA) to join our Executive Support Team, providing dedicated executive support to a member of the Senior Executive Team within one of our Faculties. This is a varied and rewarding role at the heart of the University, where no two days are the same. As a trusted member of a collaborative and experienced PA community, you will play a key role in ensuring the effective and efficient operation of the Executive's office. You will build strong working relationships with colleagues across the University and provide a high standard of administrative and organisational support in a fast-paced environment. Your responsibilities will include: Managing complex and ever-changing diaries and inboxes Coordinating meetings, preparing agendas and servicing committees Planning, organising and supporting a range of events Building and maintaining strong relationships with internal and external stakeholders Anticipating priorities and providing proactive support to ensure the smooth running of the Executive's office We're looking for someone who is confident, adaptable and enjoys working in a dynamic environment. You'll have excellent organisational skills, a keen eye for detail, outstanding communication skills, and the ability to manage multiple priorities while maintaining discretion and professionalism. Why Join Manchester Metropolitan University? At Manchester Metropolitan University, we recognise that our people are our greatest asset. We are committed to creating an inclusive, supportive, and rewarding workplace where you can thrive both professionally and personally. As part of our team, you'll benefit from: 25 days' annual leave, increasing with length of service, plus bank holidays and a University Christmas closure Hybrid working, with three days on campus and two days working from home Excellent opportunities for professional development, learning and career progression Annual salary progression (subject to scheme rules) and a range of employee reward and recognition initiatives A comprehensive benefits package including discounted gym membership, cycle to work and travel schemes, retail discounts, generous pension provision, and access to our Employee Assistance Programme to support your wellbeing If you're looking for a role where you can make a real difference while being part of a friendly, supportive, and ambitious Executive Support community, we'd love to hear from you. Application & Assessment: To apply, please submit your CV and a covering letter outlining how your skills and experience meet the requirements of the role via our online application portal. Please note that only applications includi ng a covering letter may be considered at the shortlisting stage. Assessment will include a panel-based competency interview. For an informal discussion about the role, please contact Lindsey Hall at lindsey.hall@mmu.ac.uk Further Information Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy. Documents Personal Assistant JD (1).pdf (93.18 KB) Candidate Pack 2026.pdf (9.16 MB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: Executive Support Team Salary: Grade 5 (£28,592 to £30,986) Closing Date: 18 October 2026 Contract Type: Permanent Contracted Hours per week: 35 Benefits 25 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays (Extra 5 days after 5 years of service) Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Meet the recruiter Neha Phanse ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved."
    },
    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/special-collections-assistant-9546-manchester-all-saints-campus/9442/description/": {
      "title": "Special Collections Assistant -",
      "description": "Special Collections Assistant - (9546) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Special Collections Assistant (9546) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Special Collections Assistant - (9546) Are you passionate about Special Collections and providing a brilliant service for students, and researchers? Are you looking for an opportunity to work with unique and historically significant collections within a dynamic university environment? Are you organised, detail-oriented and confident using digital systems and databases? Are you motivated by a varied role that combines public-facing work with behind-the-scenes collections management? If so, this could be the role for you. At Manchester Metropolitan University, we believe in working together as one. We are proud to create amazing spaces where colleagues can do their best work and thrive. Our Special Collections include books, objects, artworks and archives. They are a vital part of life at the University and are used extensively for teaching, research and inspiration. About the Role: As the Special Collections Assistant you will be a valued member of the Special Collections team, within the Library & Cultural Services department. You will make a significant contribution to the delivery of customer-focussed reader and enquiry services, and assist with the development, management and care of the collections. Your work will support an active engagement programme which seeks to boost engagement with academic audiences through teaching, learning and research, and with public audiences through a programme of displays and events. Key Responsibilities Deliver a high-quality customer service for Special Collections users and enquiries. Retrieve, handle and care for rare books, archives and other special collections material. Support the cataloguing, documentation and processing of collections. Assist with digitisation, metadata creation and copyright-related activities. Contribute to the preservation, storage and environmental monitoring of collections. Support the delivery of teaching sessions, exhibitions, events and reading room services. Undertake administrative tasks, data collection and reporting to support service delivery. Promote Special Collections through outreach, engagement and communications activities. Develop knowledge of the collections to support users and enhance access. This is an exciting opportunity for an individual who: Is passionate and curious about collections, and understands their potential within Higher Education Has experience of working with collections and/or archives in a museum, gallery or educational setting Is well organised, highly motivated and a brilliant communicator Enjoys working flexibly as part of a small, dedicated team Cares about providing an excellent service Why join our Library & Cultural Services? You will join a passionate and empowered team and an innovative and evolving library service. This is an exciting time to become part of our team, as we look ahead to a new landmark library building and reimagined service. Join a community that values collaboration and mutual support. Be part of a team where you can thrive and make a difference. To apply: Please submit your CV and Cover Letter, outlining your suitability to the role. Closing date Sunday 18th October 2026 Get in touch This is a fully campus-based role. For informal enquiries, please contact Jayne Evans at j.e.h.evans@mmu.ac.uk . Please note: Interviews are set to take place on 23 November . 2026 Due to high application volumes, only submissions with cover letters may be considered at shortlisting. Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy. This vacancy is expected to attract a high volume of applications. Therefore, under the Disability Confident Scheme, only disabled people who apply under the scheme and best meet the essential criteria will be offered an interview. #LI-CF1 Documents 001864.1 Special Collections Assistant Sept 2026.pdf (77.74 KB) Candidate Pack.pdf (9.16 MB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: Academic Services Salary: Grade 4 (£26,093 to £27,319) Closing Date: 18 October 2026 Contract Type: Permanent Contracted Hours per week: 35 Benefits 25 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays (Extra 5 days after 5 years of service) Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Hybrid working opportunities Meet the recruiter Claire Muir ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved."
    },
    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/technical-specialist-simulation-9570-manchester-birley-campus/9466/description/": {
      "title": "Technical Specialist (Simulation) -",
      "description": "Technical Specialist (Simulation) - (9570) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Technical Specialist (Simulation) (9570) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Technical Specialist (Simulation) - (9570) We're looking for an enthusiastic and proactive Technical Specialist in Simulation-Based Education to join our Health & Education Technical Team. This is an exciting opportunity to help shape outstanding simulated learning experiences for healthcare students, supporting teaching that develops the skills, confidence and professionalism required in practice. About the Team Technical Services provides specialist support for learning, teaching, research and enterprise activities across the University. The Health & Education Technical Team works across simulation, clinical and allied health environments, creating practical and immersive learning experiences that help students succeed. About the Role You'll play an important role in supporting and developing simulation-based education across the University. Key responsibilities include: Designing and developing engaging, simulated learning activities. Preparing and supporting specialist simulation and teaching environments. Maintaining simulation equipment and ensuring safe, effective working practices. Providing technical support, demonstrations, inductions and guidance to staff and students. Working collaboratively with colleagues to deliver an excellent technical service. Keeping up to date with developments in simulation technologies and sharing best practice. About You We're looking for someone who enjoys working in a practical, people-focused environment and is passionate about delivering high-quality learning experiences. You will bring: Experience working within a simulation facility or similar technical environment. Knowledge of simulation technologies such as high-fidelity manikins, Anatomage Tables, clinical part trainers and digital streaming systems. Understanding of Health and Safety requirements within clinical, practical or technical settings. Strong communication skills and the ability to support users with confidence and professionalism. Excellent customer service and relationship-building skills. The ability to work independently and as part of a team. Good organisational skills and the ability to manage a varied workload. Strong digital skills, including Microsoft Office, simulation software and an openness to the responsible use of AI technologies. Why Join Us? By joining our team, you'll: Be part of a friendly, skilled and supportive technical community. Help develop innovative simulation experiences for future healthcare professionals. Access training and professional development opportunities. Work in an environment that values collaboration, service excellence and continuous improvement. Join a diverse, inclusive and values-led university where everyone's contribution matters. Support a university committed to outstanding education, research and innovation. Working for Manchester Metropolitan University Manchester Metropolitan University is a forward-looking institution in the heart of the city, with excellent transport links and a commitment to supporting its people. Our benefits include: 25 days annual leave, plus Christmas closure and bank holidays. Generous pension scheme. Access to University facilities, including sports and library services. Employee Assistance Programme. Retail discounts and Cycle to Work scheme. A wide range of additional staff benefits. How to Apply To apply, please click \"Apply Now\" and complete the online application process. You will need to upload: An up-to-date CV. A covering letter (maximum one page) explaining how your skills and experience meet the essential criteria for the role. We strongly recommend reviewing the Job Description and Person Specification before submitting your application, as these documents provide full details of the role requirements and selection criteria. Further Information If you would like more information about this vacancy, please contact Antony Tibbetts, Technical Manager a.tibbetts@mmu.ac.uk This role is campus-based and requires flexibility to work across university sites where required. The post holder will normally work a shift between 08:00 and 18:00, with occasional evening or weekend working to support operational requirements. To learn more about what it's like to work at Manchester Met and the full range of colleague benefits available, please see the attached Candidate Pack below. Please note: Interviews are provisionally scheduled for the 09 & 10 November 2026 Candidates should ensure they are available to attend on one of these dates. Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Metropolitan University is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy. Documents HE_Technical_Specialist_JD_PS_Simulation_Based_Education.pdf (73.68 KB) Candidate Pack.pdf (9.16 MB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester Birley Campus Faculty / Function: Academic Services Salary: Grade 7 (£35,608 to £39,906) Closing Date: 18 October 2026 Contract Type: Permanent Contracted Hours per week: 35 Benefits 25 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays (Extra 5 days after 5 years of service) Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Meet the recruiter Claire Muir ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved."
    },
    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/web-projects-executive-9557-manchester-all-saints-campus/9453/description/": {
      "title": "Web Projects Executive",
      "description": "Web Projects Executive - (9557) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Web Projects Executive (9557) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Web Projects Executive - (9557) Manchester Metropolitan is a thriving modern university. We reach and engage with millions of people every year, and our website and digital marketing play a significant part in delivering this. We are looking for a Web Projects Executive to join our digital marketing function, driving improvement in the University's digital estate and playing a vital role in developing our websites and content management systems. This is a fantastic opportunity for someone who wants to pursue a career in digital, in particular within the product management career pathway. In the role, you will: support the ongoing development of our web estate through the entire product life cycle; scoping requirements, liaising with developers, managing the sprint process, and testing prior to release work with key stakeholders, content owners and technical specialists to understand our web performance and develop new ideas to improve the user experience undertake day-to-day tasks and administration such as supporting colleagues with queries, administering the content management system, and working with colleagues who own individual websites support team-wide initiatives such as user research or major revamps of content manage relationships with partner agencies To learn more about this exciting opportunity and benefits we offer, please read the JD and Candidate Pack provided below. About you Above all you'll be a passionate advocate for digital and its ability to support transformation and innovation. Ideally you'll already be working in the digital space, maybe already on the digital product management track, or working in account management with an agency, or be a technical specialist looking for a change of role. You will need to show us you: have an understanding of the skills and disciplines essential for product management, including agile methodologies, stakeholder engagement and supporting the development and prioritisation of product backlogs can effectively manage competing priorities to deliver outcomes in agreed timescales can work with a wide variety of stakeholders to shape business requirements which translate into a product roadmap and backlog understand user-centred design, the tools and the approaches which enable an organisation to develop a digital estate which is grounded in user needs are comfortable analysing data and user feedback to identify opportunities for improvement can work effectively with technical specialists, translating business and user needs into work packets This is the perfect role for an innovative and creative digital practitioner who wants to develop their career. About the team You will join a specialist digital team in the central marketing department. The role will work closely with a number of teams across the University. We're ambitious and driven, open to ideas and above all want to help the University and its stakeholders succeed through digital best practice. We lead the in-house digital marketing service, developing the University's web estate, working on a wide range of diverse campaigns and producing outstanding content. You'll work closely, not only with colleagues in creative, digital and marketing, but with others specialising in international or research marketing. Our work plays a key part in engaging with our many audiences, so helping the University achieve its objectives. This is currently a hybrid role, working between our campus in central Manchester and home. Application & Assessment Process: To apply, please submit a CV and covering letter detailing your suitability, on the application portal. Due to the volume of applications, we receive, we sometimes close our vacancies early. It is therefore advisable to apply as early as possible if you would like to be considered for a role. For informal enquiries, about this vacancy, please contact Ben Mitchell on B.Mitchell@mmu.ac.uk Interviews will be held in the w/c 02 November. If you would like to join our people and share our ambition, we would love to hear from you! Further Information Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the Job Description for that vacancy. This vacancy is expected to attract a high volume of applications. Therefore, under the Disability Confident Scheme, only disabled people who apply under the scheme and best meet the essential criteria will be offered an interview. Documents 000383.3 Web Projects Executive.pdf (122.55 KB) Candidate Pack.pdf (9.15 MB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: External Relations Salary: Grade 6 (£31,236 to £34,610) Closing Date: 18 October 2026 Contract Type: Permanent Contracted Hours per week: 35 Benefits 25 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays (Extra 5 days after 5 years of service) Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Hybrid working opportunities Meet the recruiter Neha Phanse ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved. Cookie Preferences This site uses cookies and other tracking technologies to improve your browsing experience, show personalised content/ads and analyse site traffic. Select cookies to accept Required cookies These cookies are used to ensure the user has a secure journey through the site. earcusessionid - Used to maintain your session. earcusession - Used to secure your session. earcucc - Used to manage your cookie preferences. Analytics Cookies Analytics cookies or performance cookies are used to track website visitors and