    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/associate-director-complex-safeguarding-and-risk-student-services-9581-manchester-all-saints-campus/9477/description/": {
      "title": "Associate Director Complex Safeguarding and Risk Student Services -",
      "description": "Associate Director Complex Safeguarding and Risk Student Services - (9581) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Associate Director Complex Safeguarding and Risk Student Services (9581) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Associate Director Complex Safeguarding and Risk Student Services - (9581) Are you an experienced strategic leader with the judgement, credibility and resilience to lead in complex and high-risk environments? Can you provide confident leadership in safeguarding, risk management and critical incident response, while building strong partnerships across a large and diverse organisation? Student wellbeing, safeguarding and risk management are more important than ever within higher education. Manchester Met is committed to providing a safe, inclusive and supportive environment where students can thrive, and we are seeking an exceptional leader to help shape and strengthen our approach. We are looking for an outstanding leader to join Student Services as Associate Director of Student Safeguarding and Complex Risk. This is a significant new role that will provide institutional leadership for safeguarding, complex student cases and critical incident management, ensuring that risk is identified, managed and escalated effectively across the University. Working closely with the Director of Student Services and senior colleagues, you will play a central role in protecting students, enhancing institutionalpractice and driving continuous improvement. About us We have been proudly driving progress for more than two centuries. As one of the UK's largest and most popular universities, we're a force for good, dedicated to delivered outstanding research and excellent education. Much more than a university, we are a place where ambitious people unite as a diverse and inclusive community to make meaningful connections. Where world-class facilities combine with exceptional minds to improve lives through innovation. We welcome those who are committed, talented, and hardworking. People who believe in our values and are as driven as we are to achieve shared goals. Our community of over 5,100 colleagues work in close partnership every day to bring about positive change regionally, nationally, and globally. Build a role with purpose, in an environment designed to unlock your potential. Be part of Manchester Met. Be Manchester Met proud. Let's transform lives together. About the role As a key member of the Student Services Leadership Team, you will provide strategic and operational leadership for safeguarding and complex risk management across the University. You will act as the University's senior operational lead for safeguarding and complex student cases, providing oversight of high-risk situations and ensuring effective coordination between services. As the Designated Safeguarding Lead Officer, you will lead the operational safeguarding framework, drive consistency of practice and provide expert advice to senior leaders on complex and sensitive matters. You will have responsibility for: Safeguarding leadership and assurance where you will oversee the implementation and continuous improvement of safeguarding frameworks, provide institutional oversight of safeguarding activity, and ensure compliance with legal, regulatory and policy requirements. Complex risk and case management where you will lead the oversight and coordination of high-risk student cases, chair risk panels, direct action where risk thresholds are met and ensure appropriate escalation of institutional risks. Critical incident response and institutional resilience where you will provide operational leadership during student-related emergencies and critical incidents, coordinate multi-service responses and support the University in managing significant welfare, safety and reputational risks. Building strong relationships across the University and with external agencies and partners, influencing strategic decision-making and ensuring a culture of shared responsibility for student safety, safeguarding and wellbeing. About You You are an inclusive and highly credible leader with substantial experience of safeguarding, complex risk management and leading services within a large complex organisation and in challenging and sensitive environments. You combine sound professional judgement with the ability to make effective decisions under pressure, navigating complexity with confidence and integrity. With a successful track record of senior leadership, within a relevant field of expertise, you have extensive experience of managing high-risk and complex cases, leading responses to critical incidents and working effectively with multiple stakeholders and external agencies. You understand the challenges facing higher education and have a strong grasp of safeguarding, welfare, mental health and institutional risk management within the HE environment. You are skilled at building productive relationships, influencing senior colleagues and providing constructive challenge where required. You can translate strategic priorities into effective operational practice and are committed to fostering a culture of collaboration, accountability and continuous improvement. Analytical and future-focused, you use insight, evidence and professional expertise to identify emerging risks, inform decision-making and improve outcomes for students and the University. Further information and how to apply To explore the post or to ask any questions you may have, please contact Jenny Clough, Director of Student Services, at j.clough@mmu.ac.uk Applications must be made via our recruitment system and should include a full CV and a letter of application setting out your interest in the role and details of how your knowledge, skills and experience match the essential criteria being sought. Interviews will be held in Manchester on Tuesday 24 November 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy. #LI-CF1 Documents Associate Director Complex Safeguarding and Risk - Student Services.pdf (294.94 KB) Rewards and Benefits Brochure.pdf (2.36 MB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: Academic Services Closing Date: 25 October 2026 Contract Type: Permanent Contracted Hours per week: 37 Benefits Meet the recruiter Carlos Favario ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved."
    },
    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/education-manager-poetry-library-9531-manchester-all-saints-campus/9428/description/": {
      "title": "Education Manager (Poetry Library)",
      "description": "Education Manager (Poetry Library) - (9531) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Education Manager (Poetry Library) (9531) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Education Manager (Poetry Library) - (9531) Are you passionate about high-quality and inclusive poetry experiences for children, young people and educators? At Manchester Metropolitan University, we believe in working together as one. We are proud to create amazing spaces where colleagues can do their best work and thrive. Join our diverse team that supports each other and is dedicated to excellence. In 2021, Manchester Met opened the North West's first public Manchester Poetry Library (MPL). Our department of Library & Cultural Services is seeking a dynamic Education Manager to join the Poetry Library team. In this position, you will work with poets, students, staff and a wide range of schools and partners to play a pivotal role in supporting poetry and literature events with Manchester Poetry Library that are open to all. About the Role: As the Education Manager you will be responsible for the organisation, facilitation and evaluation of Manchester Poetry Library's (MPL) year-round Learning programme, including strategic partnerships and projects with schools, colleges and community partners. The role will: manage and coordinate projects and outreach activities inspired by our poetry collections, including our poetry with, for, and by, children and our multilingual poetry collection work closely with schools, teachers and education professionals to design and produce CPD resources, materials, and delivery of activities, ensuring efficient and effective high-quality programmes and activities focus on inclusive opportunities that engage non-traditional arts and heritage attenders, with reader and writer development opportunities that understand and overcome barriers to engagement This is an exciting opportunity for a highly motivated individual who: has experience of working in literature, libraries, heritage, museums, archive learning or outreach and collaborative working with school and communities, not for profit and public sector is desirable is passionate about promoting inclusive poetry and literature events with children, young people and teachers and educators. has a commitment to working with people to enhance lives through co-curation, co –production, and collaborative support and partnerships. thrives in a fast-paced and inclusive environment. is an experienced project manager with excellent communication, and interpersonal skills. Hybrid working is offered for this role, where you will be able to work a proportion of time on campus and a proportion remotely. We recognise the benefits and importance of an environment that supports flexible working and are open to conversations throughout the application process. Why join our Library & Cultural Services? You will join a passionate and empowered team and an innovative and evolving library service. This is an exciting time to become part of our team, as we prepare for our Library Transformation Programme (LTP) and look ahead to a new landmark library building and reimagined service. Join a community that values collaboration and mutual support. Be part of a team where you can thrive and make a difference. To apply: Please submit your CV and Cover Letter , outlining your suitability to the role. Closing date: 25 October 2026 Please note: Interviews are scheduled to take place on Monday 30 November 2026 . We strongly recommend keeping this date available, as we may not be able to accommodate requests to reschedule interviews. Due to high application volumes, only submissions with cover letters may be considered at shortlisting. Further information: Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy. This vacancy is expected to attract a high volume of applications. Therefore, under the Disability Confident Scheme, only disabled people who apply under the scheme and best meet the essential criteria will be offered an interview. Documents Job Description.pdf (76.58 KB) Candidate Pack.pdf (9.16 MB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: Academic Services Salary: Grade 7 (£35,608 to £39,906) Closing Date: 25 October 2026 Contract Type: Permanent Contracted Hours per week: 35 Benefits 25 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays (Extra 5 days after 5 years of service) Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Hybrid working opportunities Meet the recruiter Claire Muir ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved. Cookie Preferences This site uses cookies and other tracking technologies to improve your browsing experience, show personalised content/ads and analyse site traffic. Select cookies to accept Required cookies These cookies are used to ensure the user has a secure journey through the site. earcusessionid - Used to maintain your session. earcusession - Used to secure your session. earcucc - Used to manage your cookie preferences. Analytics Cookies Analytics cookies or performance cookies are used to track website visitors and their user behaviour. _ga - Used by Google Analytics. _gid - Used by Google Analytics. _gat - Used by Google Analytics. _fbp - Used by Meta (Facebook) Pixel. Accept Cookies Accept All Cookies Customise Cookies Reject All Optional"
    },
    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/talent-and-recruitment-specialist--9590-manchester-all-saints-campus/9486/description/": {
      "title": "Talent and Recruitment Specialist -",
      "description": "Talent and Recruitment Specialist  - (9590) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Talent and Recruitment Specialist  (9590) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Talent and Recruitment Specialist  - (9590) Talent and Recruitment Specialist – People and Organisational Development Help exceptional people find meaningful careers Why join us Play a vital role in one of the UK's largest universities, at the heart of a vibrant, ambitious and globally connected city. As part of our Talent and Recruitment team, you'll help shape the future of Manchester Met by attracting the people who will drive innovation, support our students and contribute to our Road to 2035 strategy. This role is an opportunity to combine your recruitment expertise with meaningful work that creates lasting impact across our University community. At Manchester Met, we're transforming lives together. Every appointment you make, every hiring manager you support and every candidate you engage will contribute to a university that advances knowledge, benefits society and creates opportunity. What you will do As a Talent and Recruitment Specialist, you'll be a trusted partner to Faculties and Professional Services departments, delivering an exceptional recruitment experience from vacancy approval through to offer. You'll use your expertise to advise, influence and challenge, ensuring we attract talented and diverse candidates through fair, inclusive and effective recruitment practices. You will Lead end-to-end recruitment activity across a varied portfolio of vacancies. Build strong relationships with hiring managers and become their go-to recruitment expert. Advise on attraction strategies, routes to market and selection methods that deliver results. Champion inclusive recruitment practices and support initiatives that strengthen diversity across the University. Deliver inclusive recruitment and selection training to hiring managers, helping them make confident and informed hiring decisions. Use recruitment data and market insight to identify trends, improve performance and enhance service delivery. Work collaboratively with HR colleagues and external partners to continuously improve the candidate and hiring manager experience. This is more than recruitment delivery. It's an opportunity to influence strategy, improve processes and help the University attract the talent it needs to succeed. Who we are looking for You're a relationship-builder who enjoys partnering with stakeholders and providing expert advice. You combine commercial awareness with a customer-focused mindset and understand how great recruitment can support organisational success. We're particularly interested in people who bring: Experience managing end-to-end recruitment in a busy, complex environment. Strong knowledge of recruitment best practice, attraction methods and market trends. A genuine passion for inclusive recruitment and increasing the diversity of talent pipelines. The confidence to influence, advise and build credibility with stakeholders at all levels. Strong analytical skills and the ability to turn data into meaningful recommendations. Experience using ATS platforms, HR systems and reporting tools. Most importantly, you'll bring energy, curiosity and a commitment to delivering an outstanding experience for every candidate and hiring manager you support. What you will receive At Manchester Met, you'll join an inclusive, people-led culture where your development matters. We'll invest in your growth and provide the support, autonomy and opportunities you need to build a rewarding career. You'll benefit from: Generous annual leave entitlement. Competitive pension scheme. Professional and leadership development opportunities. Flexible and hybrid working options. Wellbeing support and employee assistance resources. Access to colleague networks and a collaborative University community. Discover a career with real impact Choose a career where you can achieve real-world results, transform lives and contribute to society. Join a university that values your expertise, supports your ambition and empowers you to make a difference every day. Be part of Manchester Met. Be Manchester Met proud. Let's transform lives together. Please note that shortlisting for this vacancy will take place w/c 26th October 2026 . Interviews will be held w/c 2nd November 2026. We encourage candidates to make note of these dates in the event that you are successfully invited to interview for the position. Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy. LI-MP1 Documents Talent and Recruitment Specialist - 09.10.2026.pdf (266.41 KB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: People & Organisational Development Salary: Grade 7 (£36,320 to £40,704) per annum Closing Date: 25 October 2026 Contract Type: Permanent Contracted Hours per week: 1.0 FTE Benefits 25 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays (Extra 5 days after 5 years of service) Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Meet the recruiter Michael Platt ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved."
    },
    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/lecturer-in-accounting-and-finance-9260-manchester-all-saints-campus/9169/description/": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Accounting and Finance -",
      "description": "Lecturer in Accounting and Finance - (9260) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Lecturer in Accounting and Finance (9260) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Lecturer in Accounting and Finance - (9260) Interested in making a change from industry? Do you have a passion for working with students? If so, why not join our Department of Finance and Economics. About You We are seeking enthusiastic and forward-thinking academics to join us as lecturers in accounting and finance. We want to speak to people with relevant subject expertise, a passion for developing others and creative and collaborative mindsets. You will: Have a strong industry background in Corporate Reporting & Assurance, Financial Strategy or Management Accounting. Hold a professional qualification from ACCA, ICAEW or CIMA Have a desire to shape our future curriculum. Be passionate about supporting students into great graduate roles. Be committed to developing your external profile and contributing to the wider academic and professional community. About Us Our department is one of the largest and most vibrant Finance and Economics departments in the UK, with over 2,000 students and more than 80 academic staff. Our triple accreditation places us in the top 1% of business schools worldwide - a mark of excellence in both education and research. We are currently focused on: Delivering a refreshed portfolio of undergraduate and postgraduate programmes. Expanding into emerging and interdisciplinary areas aligned with our strategic priorities and the future needs of graduate employers Innovating in Learning, Teaching and Assessment to meet the evolving needs of students and employers (including the integration of AI and the development of future-facing skills). Why Join Us? You'll be part of a dynamic, fast-paced department that places student success and graduate outcomes at the heart of everything we do. Collaboration is central to our culture, within the department and across the Business School, providing you with the opportunity to contribute to energetic and expert teams. If you're passionate about shaping the next generation of finance professionals and contributing to a department that values innovation, impact, and excellence, we'd love to hear from you. Please feel free to send any informal enquiries to Anna Egan (Head of Department) via a.egan@mmu.ac.uk Formal applications should be submitted via our recruitment portal. Please submit a CV and Cover Letter only. The cover letter should be no more than 300 words in length. Successful candidates will be invited to do the following: Take part in an interview with members of the department's senior leadership team. Deliver a 15 min presentation (with an additional 10 min Q&A time) to members of the department on a topic of the department's choosing. Find out more about our story and explore our campus ! Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy. #LI-CF1 Documents 9260 Lecturer in Accounting and Finance EPC1.pdf (196.16 KB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: Business & Law Salary: Grade 8 Closing Date: 27 October 2026 Contract Type: Permanent Contracted Hours per week: 37 Benefits 35 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Meet the recruiter Neha Phanse ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved."
    },
