rs also benefit from opportunities to support department initiatives focused on our student success priorities, including graduate outcomes and student satisfaction. The nature of this role allows the successful candidate to really immerse themselves in the department as a result of the volume of on-campus activity they will contribute too. Please note that this is a fractional role, equivalent to 0.5FTE. For informal discussion about the role please contact Anna Egan (Head of Department) at a.egan@mmu.ac.uk Interested applicants should submit a CV and a cover letter (max 1 page) outlining how their experience aligns with the above identified requirements of the role. Why Join Manchester Met? At Manchester Metropolitan University , we are proud to foster an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity, celebrates diversity, and values the different perspectives a diverse workforce brings. We warmly encourage applications from all communities, including candidates from Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, and are committed to ensuring colleagues can thrive in their roles. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or employment, we will work with you to provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusion is reflected through mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities designed to empower underrepresented groups. As a Disability Confident Leader , Manchester Met aims to offer an interview to disabled applicants who meet the essential criteria outlined in the Job Description #LI-CF1 Documents 9257 Academic Tutor.pdf (274.24 KB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: Business & Law Salary: Grade 7 Closing Date: 27 October 2026 Contract Type: Permanent Contracted Hours per week: 17.5 Benefits 35 days leave + Ch