    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/hourly-paid-worker-tutor-soda--9579-manchester-all-saints-campus/9475/description/": {
      "title": "Hourly Paid Worker Tutor (SODA)",
      "description": "Hourly Paid Worker Tutor (SODA)  - (9579) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Hourly Paid Worker Tutor (SODA)  (9579) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Hourly Paid Worker Tutor (SODA)  - (9579) Manchester Metropolitan University is one of the UK's most inspiring higher education institutions, offering the opportunity for passionate and committed individuals to make a difference to the lives of people and communities locally, nationally and internationally.  We have a clear vision, a compelling strategy and our ambition is simple: to be the best modern university in the sector, where students and staff alike are equipped with every resource to excel. Manchester Metropolitan University has been a pioneer in modern education since its origins in 1824. Hourly Paid Associates/workers (Teaching Related) We are looking to engage with academic professionals across a wide range of different specialisms on an hourly paid basis. These hours are available on a short term, ad hoc basis providing support to our students through a range of roles.  You will have experience in delivering and supporting Higher Education activities, at an undergraduate and postgraduate level, in subject specific and interdisciplinary contexts or have strong relevant industry knowledge and experience. You will have a positive approach and the ability to contribute to a team. The School of Digital Arts The School of Digital Arts within Manchester School of Art is a purpose built, interdisciplinary school offering industry and research informed courses and specialist spaces with the latest technologies. Our students study disciplines that span film, animation, UX, photography, games design, games art and more, often working on live projects with industry partners and frequently collaborating with fellow students and researchers. They choose from a flexible mix of courses: foundation year, undergraduate, postgraduate and research degrees that run alongside degree apprenticeships, summer schools and short courses. We are looking for Hourly Paid Tutors (Teaching Related) to join our SODA teaching Talent Pool across the following disciplines: Animation Games Art Games Design Filmmaking Photography Future Media Production Music and Sound Design User Experience Design Interdisciplinary digital arts As an Hourly Paid Associate/ Worker in these roles you are required to have: Excellent communication skills and interpersonal skills. The ability to plan and prioritise workload to meet objectives. The ability to use initiative when dealing with a wide range of issues and problems, challenging decisions appropriately. A degree or appropriate equivalent experience in your subject area, along with knowledge and understanding of the changing nature of HE To Apply: Please attach a CV detailing your professional and any teaching experience, making it clear which discipline/s you would like to be considered for. Working at Manchester Met: Manchester Metropolitan University is a great place to work, and you will be part of a great team.  We are ambitious for ourselves as an academic institution, and for both our students and our colleagues. In addition to a great working environment, you will have access to the University facilities including sport and library. If you would like to join our people and share our ambition, we would love to hear from you. Please submit your CV and covering letter via our application portal where once reviewed a member of the Resourcing team will be in contact to discuss next steps. Please note that if we have no suitable hours available immediately, we will ask to retain your details in our talent pool for future opportunities. Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy. Documents Hourly Paid Worker - Tutor JD.pdf (283.03 KB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: Arts & Humanities Benefits Meet the recruiter Michelle Legg ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved. Cookie Preferences This site uses cookies and other tracking technologies to improve your browsing experience, show personalised content/ads and analyse site traffic. Select cookies to accept Required cookies These cookies are used to ensure the user has a secure journey through the site. earcusessionid - Used to maintain your session. earcusession - Used to secure your session. earcucc - Used to manage your cookie preferences. Analytics Cookies Analytics cookies or performance cookies are used to track website visitors and their user behaviour. _ga - Used by Google Analytics. _gid - Used by Google Analytics. _gat - Used by Google Analytics. _fbp - Used by Meta (Facebook) Pixel. Accept Cookies Accept All Cookies Customise Cookies Reject All Optional"
    },
    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/digital-librarian-9602-manchester-all-saints-campus/9498/description/": {
      "title": "Digital Librarian",
      "description": "Digital Librarian - (9602) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Digital Librarian (9602) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Digital Librarian - (9602) Are you passionate about improving digital services and creating seamless access to knowledge, culture and research? Manchester Metropolitan University Library & Cultural Services is seeking an ambitious and innovative Digital Librarian to join our Digital Services team. This is an exciting opportunity to play a leading role in developing and enhancing the systems, platforms and services that underpin access to our library, cultural and research collections. As we continue to transform our digital services and explore new opportunities through emerging technologies, AI and automation, we are looking for someone who enjoys solving problems, working collaboratively and using technology to improve the experience of students, researchers and staff. About us Library & Cultural Services supports teaching, learning and research across the University and holds a rich and diverse range of collections, including Library resources, Special Collections, the Poetry Library and the North West Film Archive. We are delivering ambitious plans to modernise our systems and services, ensuring our digital services remain innovative, sustainable and responsive to changing user needs. As part of one of the UK's largest universities, you will join a collaborative and forward-looking team, working alongside colleagues across Professional Services and cultural heritage sectors to create exceptional digital experiences for our community. About the role Reporting to the Digital Services Manager, you will play a key role in the development, implementation and continuous improvement of the platforms, systems and services that support discovery, access and engagement across Library & Cultural Services. Your responsibilities will include: Supporting the development and management of library and cultural services systems, digital platforms, websites, applications and databases. Leading the delivery and continuous improvement of electronic resources and digital collections to ensure reliable and seamless access. Contributing expertise in areas such as metadata, discovery services, websites and digital content management. Using data, user insight and UX approaches to inform decision making and improve services. Exploring opportunities to use emerging technologies, AI and automation to enhance service delivery and operational efficiency. You will also contribute to projects that support strategic priorities across Library & Cultural Services, helping to shape the future of our digital infrastructure and ensuring services remain accessible, user-focused and aligned to the needs of teaching, learning and research. About you You will be an experienced library or information professional with a strong interest in digital services, systems and technologies. You will enjoy analysing problems, identifying opportunities for improvement and working collaboratively with a wide range of colleagues and stakeholders. We are looking for someone who can demonstrate: Experience of working with library or cultural services systems, discovery platforms, repositories or related digital services. Enthusiasm for innovation and the potential of new technologies to transform library services. Strong communication and relationship-building skills. Excellent organisational skills and the ability to manage competing priorities. A commitment to delivering excellent customer service and continuously improving the user experience. Most importantly, you will be excited by the opportunity to help shape the future of digital library and cultural services within a large and ambitious university. Further information and how to apply For any enquiries please contact Emily Shields, Digital Services Manager , at e.shields@mmu.ac.uk Applications must be made via our recruitment system and should include a full CV and a supporting statement , of no more than 2 sides of A4, outlining how your knowledge, skills and experience meet the requirements of the role. Interviews are expected to be held on Tuesday 24 November (24/11/2026). Candidates should keep this date free where possible, as alternative interview dates may not be available. Hybrid working is offered for this role, where you will be able to work a proportion of time on campus and a proportion remotely. Equality and diversity commitment At Manchester Metropolitan University Library, we are committed to fostering an inclusive environment that centres diversity and promotes equality. We actively encourage applications from candidates of all backgrounds, regardless of ethnicity, sex, gender, sexual orientation, disability, age, or religion. We believe that a diverse and inclusive workforce enhances our ability to meet the diverse needs of our academic community. As a Digital Librarian, you will play your part in championing equality and diversity, contributing to a positive and respectful workplace culture. We are working on making our recruitment process as inclusive as we can, and welcome any queries or feedback. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and this vacancy is expected to attract a high volume of applications. Therefore, under the Disability Confident Scheme, only disabled people who apply under the scheme and best meet the essential criteria will be offered an interview. Documents Candidate Pack.pdf (9.16 MB) 001845.3 Digital Librarian (1).pdf (125.92 KB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: Academic Services Salary: Grade 7 (£36,320 to £40,704) Closing Date: 27 October 2026 Contract Type: Permanent Contracted Hours per week: 35 Benefits 25 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays (Extra 5 days after 5 years of service) Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Hybrid working opportunities Meet the recruiter Claire Muir ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved. Cookie Preferences This site uses cookies and other tracking technologies to improve your browsing experience, show personalised content/ads and analyse site traffic. Select cookies to accept Required cookies These cookies are used to ensure the user has a secure journey through the site. earcusessionid - Used to maintain your session. earcusession - Used to secure your session. earcucc - Used to manage your cookie preferences. Analytics Cookies Analytics cookies or performance cookies are used to track website visitors and their user behaviour. _ga - Used by Google Analytics. _gid - Used by Google Analytics. _gat - Used by Google Analytics. _fbp - Used by Meta (Facebook) Pixel. Accept Cookies Accept All Cookies Customise Cookies Reject All Optional"
    },
    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/hr-administrator--9615-manchester-all-saints-campus/9511/description/": {
      "title": "HR Administrator",
      "description": "HR Administrator  - (9615) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - HR Administrator  (9615) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login HR Administrator  - (9615) Build a Meaningful Career Supporting People at Manchester Met Why join us? Become part of our collaborative culture, diverse teams and well-connected community. At Manchester Metropolitan University, we believe in working together, sharing knowledge and valuing everyone's contribution. As an HR Administrator, you'll play a vital role in supporting colleagues and candidates throughout their journey with us, helping to create positive experiences that enable our people to thrive and helping us in our commitment to transforming lives together. Working at one of the UK's largest universities, you'll join an award-winning workplace with a strong focus on people, inclusion and career development. You'll be part of a team that keeps our people processes running smoothly while making a genuine difference to colleagues across the University. What you'll do No two days are the same in our HR Service Centre. You'll provide operational and administrative support across the full employee lifecycle, helping to deliver an efficient, responsive and high-quality HR service. Your responsibilities will include: Coordinating recruitment activity, including interview scheduling, candidate communications and offer administration. Supporting onboarding and pre-employment checks, including Right to Work verification and compliance processes. Creating, maintaining and updating employee records across University systems including Oracle and SharePoint. Acting as a first point of contact for HR queries, delivering accurate and timely advice while escalating complex matters appropriately. Managing team inboxes, handling enquiries and helping colleagues and managers access the support they need. Supporting family leave, absence management, contractual changes and other core HR processes. Contributing to a positive candidate and employee experience at every stage of the recruitment and employment journey. Who we're looking for You're an organised and customer-focused administrator who enjoys working in a fast-paced environment and takes pride in delivering an excellent service. You'll be confident managing multiple priorities, building positive relationships and maintaining high levels of accuracy. We're particularly interested in hearing from people who can demonstrate: Excellent administrative, organisational and communication skills. Strong attention to detail and the ability to manage competing priorities. Experience delivering high levels of customer service. Confidence using Microsoft Office applications, including Excel. Experience working in an HR, recruitment or similar administrative environment. An ability to communicate professionally and sensitively with a wide range of stakeholders. A commitment to equality, diversity, inclusion and continuous personal development. What you'll receive In return, you'll join a diverse and inclusive community of more than 5,000 colleagues where every voice is valued and respected. You'll have access to development opportunities, supportive colleagues and the chance to build a rewarding career at a university that is proudly driving progress and creating positive impact locally, nationally and globally. As part of the Manchester Met community, you'll benefit from: Generous annual leave entitlement. An excellent pension scheme. Flexible and hybrid working opportunities where appropriate. Career development and learning opportunities. Wellbeing support and staff networks. Retail, leisure and lifestyle discounts. Join us and make a difference Choose an impactful role and become a valued member of our welcoming and inclusive community. You'll help to deliver an outstanding experience for colleagues and candidates while developing your own skills and career with one of the UK's leading universities. Be part of Manchester Met. Be Manchester Met proud. Let's transform lives together. Further information: Closing Date: 28th October 2026 Interviews: w/c 9th and w/c 16th November Candidates are encouraged to make a note of these dates and have availability to attend interviews should you be successful during this period. Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy. This vacancy is expected to attract a high volume of applications. Therefore, under the Disability Confident Scheme, only disabled people who apply under the scheme and best meet the essential criteria will be offered an interview. #LI-MP1 Documents Professional Services Candidate Pack.pdf (9.15 MB) 000825.3 HR Administrator Grade 4 (new JD evaluated by Reward) (1) (1).pdf (264.26 KB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: People & Organisational Development Salary: £26,615 to £27,865 per annum Closing Date: 28 October 2026 Contract Type: Permanent Contracted Hours per week: 35 hours per week Benefits 25 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays (Extra 5 days after 5 years of service) Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Hybrid working opportunities Meet the recruiter Michael Platt ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved. Cookie Preferences This site uses cookies and other tracking technologies to improve your browsing experience, show personalised content/ads and analyse site traffic. Select cookies to accept Required cookies These cookies are used to ensure the user has a secure journey through the site. earcusessionid - Used to maintain your session. earcusession - Used to secure your session. earcucc - Used to manage your cookie preferences. Analytics Cookies Analytics cookies or performance cookies are used to track website visitors and their user behaviour. _ga - Used by Google Analytics. _gid - Used by Google Analytics. _gat - Used by Google Analytics. _fbp - Used by Meta (Facebook) Pixel. Accept Cookies Accept All Cookies Customise Cookies Reject All Optional"
    },
    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/lecturer-architecture---continuity-atelier-9624-manchester-all-saints-campus/9520/description/": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Architecture",
      "description": "Lecturer (Architecture - Continuity Atelier) - (9624) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Lecturer (Architecture - Continuity Atelier) (9624) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Lecturer (Architecture - Continuity Atelier) - (9624) 7 HOURS PER WEEK UNTIL 8 th JUNE 2027 (TUESDAY) The Manchester School of Architecture is ranked 5 th in the prestigious QS world university rankings and enjoys the unique context of being a collaboration between Manchester Metropolitan University and the University of Manchester. It is one of the largest Schools of Architecture in the country with over 1000 students (typically representing some 85 countries) and over 150 staff from diverse backgrounds and is proud to retain both its quality and sense of community despite its size. The School is characterised by excellence, ambition, boldness, inquisitiveness, innovation, and social justice and responsibility. These facets generate a unique blend and balance between research led teaching, impressive and relevant research outputs and extensive professional industry links, all of which encourage our students to cultivate their own unique approach to architecture and their careers thereafter. The specific role is as a Lecturer in the Continuity Atelier which was established in 1993 as Continuity in Architecture, a studio for research informed teaching, that specialises in the sustainable adaptation of buildings, landscape and urban space within historic contexts. The Atelier believes that an elemental approach to studying architectural and landscape technology within historic settings has never been more pressing. Inspired by our forebears' systematic analysis of contextual resource – their application of ready means and traditional craft techniques originating from vibrant environments, we strive to rediscover sustainable, layered, nuanced, contextual and environmentally appropriate solutions for our time.  Continuity is interested in the distinct relationships buildings and landscapes have with climate and place and how they can express the nature of a region and represent a particular culture or situation. It is interested in the articulation of space; how interiors and the exteriors interrelate, whether explicit or not, and how spaces can be grouped or connected to form complex environments. It is also interested in why buildings and landscapes are designed and their morphology, along with detail - how intimate details and the expression of connections reinforce and characterise the whole. You will be responsible for solely representing the Atelier on a new, additional studio day which provides third year students with a holistic studio day to develop their design projects. The role requires a strong understanding the design process, a holistic approach to architectural design and construction, and the profession of architecture. Due to the independent nature of the role it will be important for the successful candidate to have significant teaching experience in design studio, a well-rounded knowledge of the PSRB curriculum, and experience of leading and orgnanising studio activities. You will also have exceptional inter-personal and communication qualities, excellent organisational and administrative skills, and a collaborative approach to working. We will also look to you to ensure an excellent student experience through the use of relevant and inspiring learning and teaching. This post is for one day a week and so will not support a visa application. Only candidates with the right to work in the UK are eligible to apply. Informal discussions can be held with Atelier leader John Lee via john.lee@mmu.ac.uk Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy. Documents Job Description.pdf (226.25 KB) Candidate Pack.pdf (9.15 MB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: Arts & Humanities Salary: Grade 8 (£41,885 to £48,337) Closing Date: 28 October 2026 Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract Length: ends 8th June 2027 Contracted Hours per week: 7 Benefits 35 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Meet the recruiter Michelle Legg ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved."
    },
    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/lecturer-in-architecture--continuity-atelier-9623-manchester-all-saints-campus/9519/description/": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Architecture (Continuity Atelier) -",
      "description": "Lecturer in Architecture  (Continuity Atelier) - (9623) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Lecturer in Architecture  (Continuity Atelier) (9623) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Lecturer in Architecture  (Continuity Atelier) - (9623) 7 HOURS PER WEEK UNTIL 10 th JUNE 2027 (THURSDAY) The Manchester School of Architecture is ranked 5 th in the prestigious QS world university rankings and enjoys the unique context of being a collaboration between Manchester Metropolitan University and the University of Manchester. It is one of the largest Schools of Architecture in the country with over 1000 students (typically representing some 85 countries) and over 150 staff from diverse backgrounds and is proud to retain both its quality and sense of community despite its size. The School is characterised by excellence, ambition, boldness, inquisitiveness, innovation, and social justice and responsibility. These facets generate a unique blend and balance between research led teaching, impressive and relevant research outputs and extensive professional industry links, all of which encourage our students to cultivate their own unique approach to architecture and their careers thereafter. The specific role is as a Lecturer in the Continuity Atelier which was established in 1993 as Continuity in Architecture, a studio for research informed teaching, that specialises in the sustainable adaptation of buildings, landscape and urban space within historic contexts. The Atelier believes that an elemental approach to studying architectural and landscape technology within historic settings has never been more pressing. Inspired by our forebears' systematic analysis of contextual resource – their application of ready means and traditional craft techniques originating from vibrant environments, we strive to rediscover sustainable, layered, nuanced, contextual and environmentally appropriate solutions for our time.  Continuity is interested in the distinct relationships buildings and landscapes have with climate and place and how they can express the nature of a region and represent a particular culture or situation. It is interested in the articulation of space; how interiors and the exteriors interrelate, whether explicit or not, and how spaces can be grouped or connected to form complex environments. It is also interested in why buildings and landscapes are designed and their morphology, along with detail - how intimate details and the expression of connections reinforce and characterise the whole. Within the Atelier you will be responsible for the teaching the final year of the BA programme within a small team of staff. The role requires a strong understanding the design process, a holistic approach to architectural design and construction, and the profession of architecture. Some formal teaching experience is absolutely essential and you will also have exceptional inter-personal and communication qualities, excellent organisational and administrative skills, and a collaborative approach to working. We will also look to you to ensure an excellent student experience through the use of relevant and inspiring learning and teaching. This post is for one day a week and so will not support a visa application. Only candidates with the right to work in the UK are eligible to apply. Informal discussions can be held with Atelier leader John Lee via john.lee@mmu.ac.uk Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy. Documents Lecturer JD EPC Continuity Thurs cover.pdf (225.55 KB) Candidate Pack.pdf (9.15 MB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: Arts & Humanities Salary: Grade 8 (£41,885 to £48,337) pro rata Closing Date: 28 October 2026 Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract Length: ends 10th June 2027 Contracted Hours per week: 7 Benefits 35 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Hybrid working opportunities Meet the recruiter Michelle Legg ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved."
