    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/artificial-intelligence-specialist-in-manufacturing-applications-senior-research-associate-9480-other/9379/description/": {
      "title": "Artificial Intelligence Specialist in Manufacturing Applications (Senior Research Associate) -",
      "description": "Artificial Intelligence Specialist in Manufacturing Applications (Senior Research Associate) - (9480) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Artificial Intelligence Specialist in Manufacturing Applications (Senior Research Associate) (9480) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Artificial Intelligence Specialist in Manufacturing Applications (Senior Research Associate) - (9480) About the Faculty The Faculty of Science and Engineering is one of the UK's largest providers of science, engineering and technology education, combining world-leading research with innovative teaching and strong industry engagement. Our academics work across disciplines to address emerging global challenges while equipping graduates with the skills and knowledge needed to succeed in a rapidly changing world. About the School The School of Engineering and Environment brings together expertise across a broad range of engineering and environmental disciplines, delivering high-quality education, impactful research and strong industrial engagement. Engineering at our University ranked 6 th in the UK in the last REF for the impact of our research. We have real strengths in advanced materials and manufacturing in the school through our additive manufacturing facility PrintCity and our surface engineering group. About the Project The University was recently successful in securing funding to deliver the Challenge AI programme. The programme is funded by the Local Innovation Partnership Fund. ChallengeAI connects businesses with universities, researchers and industry experts through funded pathways designed to support the responsible adoption of Artificial Intelligence (AI). It will give businesses the opportunity to explore how AI could have a real impact on their business and ensure that they the support and guidance that they need to make the right decisions for their business. About the Role & Team In this role you will be based at PrintCity our award winning additive manufacturing facility. PrintCity has over 100 additive manufacturing machines and a wide range of scanning equipment. Over £3.5M has been invested in state of the art equipment and you will join a team that has worked with over 300 industry partners in the last 5 years. You will be the lead in PrintCity for the Challenge AI project and will work closely with colleagues in the Centre for Enterprise in our Business school on projects with industry focused on the responsible adoption of AI solutions for companies involved in manufacturing, production and design. Key Responsibilities Your key responsibilities will include: - Leading research and innovation projects in AI for product design,  manufacturing,  production and quality assurance for companies enrolled onto the Challenge AI programme. - Utilising AI to implement solutions in organisations, to boost productivity,  improve efficiencies  or  enhance  quality control. - Supporting  colleagues with queries related to company recruitment , triage, supporting ideation workshops with technical activities related to  AI in design, manufacturing and production. - Working with companies on the programme to develop short or long term research and innovation programmes related to the implementation of  AI solutions, supporting skills development within companies on the programme. Key Skills & Experiences You will be expected to: - Have the ability to lead the work of a research team, co-ordinating effort and resources. - Have the ability to build relationships and establish networks with internal and external contacts. Especially SMEs and large OEMs. - Have specialist knowledge of AI software, product design software, manufacturing processes (additive manufacturing in particular), and production operations. - An understanding of other industrial digital technologies and processes for example:  Industrial 3D Scanning, including software and workflows; Robotics and automation ; Machine connectivity, data extraction and custom dashboards - Have Proficiency in programming languages (Python, PHP, MySQL, etc) and API development (RESTful,GraphQL, etc). To learn more about role and requirements, please read the Job Description provided below. If you would like to join our people and share our ambition, we would love to hear from you! Application & Assessment Process: - To apply, please submit a CV (2 page maximum) and covering letter (1 page maximum) detailing your suitability, on the application portal. - Please be aware that only applications including a cover letter may be considered at shortlisting stage. - Interviews to be held in the w/c 23 November - Assessment will include delivery of presentation followed by a panel interview. We believe in working together, sharing knowledge and valuing everyone's contributions. Develop your skills, further your knowledge and be part of a team who are transforming lives, every single day! Further Information Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from local and international communities, including those from Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy. This vacancy is expected to attract a high volume of applications. Therefore, under the Disability Confident Scheme, only disabled people who apply under the scheme and best meet the essential criteria will be offered an interview. Find out more about our story and explore our campus Documents AMMIC_JD Artificial Intelligence Specialist (Manufacturing Applications)  Challenge AI.pdf (84.83 KB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Other Faculty / Function: Science & Engineering Salary: Grade 8 (£41,885 to £48,337) Closing Date: 1 November 2026 Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract Length: 3.5 years /31st March 2030 Contracted Hours per week: 37 Benefits 35 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Meet the recruiter Neha Phanse ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved."
    },
    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/emergency-planning-resilience-and-risk-systems-manager-9596-manchester-all-saints-campus/9492/description/": {
      "title": "Emergency Planning, Resilience and Risk Systems Manager",
      "description": "Emergency Planning, Resilience and Risk Systems Manager - (9596) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Emergency Planning, Resilience and Risk Systems Manager (9596) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Emergency Planning, Resilience and Risk Systems Manager - (9596) Could you help shape how Manchester Metropolitan prepares for, responds to and recovers from major incidents and disruption? We're looking for an experienced and proactive Emergency Planning, Resilience and Risk Manager to provide professional leadership across emergency planning, operational resilience, business continuity and associated risk and incident management arrangements within Estates, Facilities and Campus Development (EFCD). Reporting to the Head of Compliance, Risk and Assurance, you'll play a pivotal role in strengthening resilience across one of the University's most diverse and operationally critical directorates. About Our Team: The Compliance, Risk and Assurance Team sits within Estates, Facilities and Campus Development (EFCD) and plays a key role in supporting the safe, compliant and resilient operation of the University's buildings, infrastructure, accommodation and services. Working collaboratively across EFCD and the wider University, the team provides expertise in compliance, risk management, assurance, emergency planning and resilience. You'll join a supportive and forward-thinking team of professionals who work closely with colleagues across health and safety, fire safety, security, facilities management and governance functions to drive continuous improvement. Together, the team helps ensure that Manchester Metropolitan is well prepared to manage risk, respond effectively to incidents and maintain critical services for students, staff and visitors. About the Role: This is an exciting opportunity to lead the development, implementation and continuous improvement of EFCD's emergency planning, operational resilience, business continuity and risk management arrangements. Working with a high degree of professional autonomy, you will provide expert advice, support organisational preparedness, and help ensure risks are effectively identified, managed and escalated through the University's governance framework. Key areas of responsibility include incident management, resilience planning, business continuity, emergency response, organisational assurance and coordinating EFCD's implementation of Martyn's Law. The role operates across all EFCD services, including buildings, facilities, security operations, student accommodation, infrastructure and critical supply chains. Occasional out-of-hours attendance may be required in support of incident response activities. For a full outline of the role and responsibilities, please refer to the Job Description attached below. About You: We're looking for a highly skilled resilience, emergency planning, business continuity or risk professional who can operate confidently in a complex organisational environment. You'll be able to demonstrate: Significant experience in developing, implementing and reviewing emergency management, business continuity and risk management arrangements. Experience leading emergency planning and/or business continuity activity within a large and complex organisation. Excellent analytical, problem-solving and decision-making skills, with the ability to interpret complex information and recommend practical solutions. Strong communication, influencing and relationship-building skills, with the ability to work effectively across a wide range of stakeholders. Experience of delivering training, exercises and organisational preparedness activities. A strong understanding of professional, legal and regulatory frameworks relating to emergency preparedness, resilience and business continuity. A degree or equivalent qualification, together with relevant professional knowledge and expertise in emergency management and business continuity. Knowledge of Estates, Facilities Management or similar operational environments would be advantageous but is not essential. How to Apply: If you'd like to apply, please take the time to review the essential criteria within the Job Description and submit: An up-to-date CV A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role and how your skills and experience meet the requirements of the position For informal enquiries about the role, please contact Claudia Mendonca at c.mendonca@mmu.ac.uk . We look forward to hearing from you! Please note: interviews are provisionally expected to take place during the week commencing 16 November 2026. Candidates are encouraged to keep this period available where possible, as we may be unable to accommodate alternative interview dates. Further information: Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy. Documents 002524.1 Emergency Planning Resilience and Risk Manager.pdf (79.79 KB) Candidate Pack.pdf (9.16 MB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: Estates, Facilities and Campus Development Salary: Grade 9 (£49,798 to £57,666) Closing Date: 3 November 2026 Contract Type: Permanent Contracted Hours per week: 37 Benefits 35 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Meet the recruiter Claire Muir ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved. Cookie Preferences This site uses cookies and other tracking technologies to improve your browsing experience, show personalised content/ads and analyse site traffic. Select cookies to accept Required cookies These cookies are used to ensure the user has a secure journey through the site. earcusessionid - Used to maintain your session. earcusession - Used to secure your session. earcucc - Used to manage your cookie preferences. Analytics Cookies Analytics cookies or performance cookies are used to track website visitors and their user behaviour. _ga - Used by Google Analytics. _gid - Used by Google Analytics. _gat - Used by Google Analytics. _fbp - Used by Meta (Facebook) Pixel. Accept Cookies Accept All Cookies Customise Cookies Reject All Optional"
