    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/faculty-planning-officer-9599-manchester-all-saints-campus/9495/description/": {
      "title": "Faculty Planning Officer",
      "description": "Faculty Planning Officer - (9599) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Faculty Planning Officer (9599) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Faculty Planning Officer - (9599) Do you enjoy working with data, identifying trends and providing insights that help shape decision-making? Are you looking for an opportunity to develop your skills in planning, analysis and project work within a dynamic University environment? If so, this could be the role for you! We have an exciting opportunity for a Faculty Planning Officer to join the Faculty Planning and Operations Team within the Faculty of Science and Engineering. Reporting to the Senior Faculty Planning and Operations Manager, you will play a key role in supporting the Faculty's strategic planning processes, performance monitoring and operational delivery. A little more about the role: In this role, you will support the development and monitoring of strategic plans and key performance data across the Faculty. You will provide insightful analysis to support decision-making and help inform Faculty and Departmental priorities. Your work will include market insight analysis, project support, performance monitoring, operational planning, statutory returns and the production of management information. You will be responsible for identifying trends, interpreting complex datasets and making evidence-based recommendations to support strategic and operational objectives. We're looking for someone who has: Experience using Excel and/or Power BI, including the development and management of complex, multi-layered spreadsheets, dashboards or reports. Strong statistical and analytical skills, with the ability to interpret complex datasets and provide actionable insights. The ability to produce clear, engaging and informative reports and presentations tailored to a range of audiences. Excellent organisational skills, with a proven ability to manage competing priorities, balance workload demands and meet deadlines. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the confidence to build effective working relationships with stakeholders at all levels. Experience of undertaking data analysis and making recommendations to inform strategic decision-making. The ability to work proactively, use initiative and contribute positively within a collaborative team environment. For further information about the role and person specification, please review the Job Description , which is attached at the bottom of this screen. For an informal discussion about the role: Please contact Sean Threlfall at s.threlfall@mmu.ac.uk To apply: Upload your CV (a cover letter is not required). Complete the two mandatory application questions as part of the application form (under Supporting Information). We recommend responses of 300-500 words per question. Where possible, please structure your answers using the STAR method (Situation, Task, Action, Result) and provide specific examples that demonstrate your experience and impact. Please note: Interviews are provisionally scheduled for 17 and/or 18 November (17/11/2026 and 18/11/2026). Candidates should make every effort to be available on these dates, as alternative interview dates may not be possible. A little more about the team: You'll be joining a supportive and collaborative Faculty Planning and Operations Team that works closely with academic and professional services colleagues across the University. The team provides planning expertise, performance analysis and operational support that helps deliver Faculty and institutional priorities. The role offers an excellent opportunity to develop your knowledge of higher education planning, build a broad professional network and contribute to a range of high-profile projects and initiatives. Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy. Documents Faculty Planning Officer (G6).pdf (249.25 KB) Candidate Pack.pdf (9.16 MB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: Strategic Planning Office Salary: Grade 6 (£31,861 to £35,302) Closing Date: 2 November 2026 Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract Length: Anticipated to end 31/10/2027 Contracted Hours per week: 35 Benefits 25 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays (Extra 5 days after 5 years of service) Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Hybrid working opportunities Meet the recruiter Claire Muir ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved. Cookie Preferences This site uses cookies and other tracking technologies to improve your browsing experience, show personalised content/ads and analyse site traffic. Select cookies to accept Required cookies These cookies are used to ensure the user has a secure journey through the site. earcusessionid - Used to maintain your session. earcusession - Used to secure your session. earcucc - Used to manage your cookie preferences. Analytics Cookies Analytics cookies or performance cookies are used to track website visitors and their user behaviour. _ga - Used by Google Analytics. _gid - Used by Google Analytics. _gat - Used by Google Analytics. _fbp - Used by Meta (Facebook) Pixel. Accept Cookies Accept All Cookies Customise Cookies Reject All Optional"
