    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/sports-physiotherapist-9384-manchester-birley-campus/9292/description/": {
      "title": "Sports Physiotherapist",
      "description": "Sports Physiotherapist - (9384) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Sports Physiotherapist (9384) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Sports Physiotherapist - (9384) An exciting opportunity has arisen for a Sports Physiotherapist to join the Manchester Movement Unit on a 0.8 FTE fixed-term contract for two years. About the team: The Manchester Movement Unit provides physiotherapy services to Manchester Metropolitan University staff and students, the local community, and private clients. We also deliver specialist support to Manchester Metropolitan University Sport (MMU Sport), the Talented Athlete Scholarship Scheme (TASS), and Professional Game Referees (Pro Ref). As Manchester's only academic physiotherapy practice, we deliver evidence-based practice, clinical excellence, and patient-centred care. Our team includes two highly specialist part-time Clinic Directors, a full-time Senior Sports Physiotherapist, and a full-time Physiotherapist, all working collaboratively across our services. Due to continued growth, we are seeking a motivated and enthusiastic person who is keen to develop their skills while working alongside highly experienced clinicians. The successful candidate will manage a varied caseload of musculoskeletal and sports injury patients, including athletes supported through MMU Sport and TASS, football match officials from Pro Ref, and private clients. The role will specifically involve supporting athletes who are part of the University's football performance programme and lead emergency first aid cover at football fixtures and selected MMU Sport events. Working within this team, you will Manage your clinical caseload, support the efficient day-to-day delivery of appointments and contribute to the ongoing development of a flexible and high-quality physiotherapy service. Provide high-quality assessment, treatment, rehabilitation and follow up care for patients with musculoskeletal conditions and sports injuries. Maintain accurate, comprehensive clinical records in line with HCPC standards of professional practice. Be flexible and may be expected to work across a six-day week to provide a service across clinic operating hours, at the times of highest patient demand. Work closely with experienced colleagues and benefit from a programme of professional development and support to help you achieve high standards of clinical practice. Be supported to undertake practice educator training, allowing you to contribute to the supervision and development of physiotherapy students on clinical placement. Who we are looking for: We are seeking a highly committed and enthusiastic physiotherapist who is passionate about making a difference to people's lives. Essential requirements: A Chartered Physiotherapist, registered with the Health and Care Professions Council (HCPC) and Chartered Society of Physiotherapy. Substantial experience which must include musculoskeletal and sports physiotherapy practice. Strong clinical knowledge and physiotherapy skills, across a range of practice areas and settings. A willingness to learn and be flexible in your approach to patient care. Excellent communication, interpersonal and teamwork skills. A commitment to continuing professional development and contributing to the ongoing growth and success of the Manchester Movement Unit. Desireable requirements: Level 4 Sports Massage qualification. Level 4 Trauma Management qualification (for example, FA Intermediate Trauma Medical Management in Football or equivalent). To apply: Do you have the qualities we are looking for? Are you looking to take the next step in your physiotherapy career? Please submit your CV and Cover Letter outlining your suitability to the role. For an informal discussion about the role, please contact Dr Tom Hughes or Dr Chris McCarthy, t.hughes@mmu.ac.uk & chris.mccarthy@mmu.ac.uk Please note: Applications close on Monday 2 nd November at 11.59pm and interviews are scheduled to take place shortly thereafter in November. Further information: Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy. #LI-MP1 Documents V2 001683.1 Sport Physiotherapist.pdf (250.84 KB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester Birley Campus Faculty / Function: Health & Education Salary: Grade 6 (£31,236 to £34,610) pro rata Closing Date: 2 November 2026 Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract Length: 2 years 30/09/2028 Contracted Hours per week: 0.8 Benefits 25 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays (Extra 5 days after 5 years of service) Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Meet the recruiter Michael Platt ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved. Cookie Preferences This site uses cookies and other tracking technologies to improve your browsing experience, show personalised content/ads and analyse site traffic. Select cookies to accept Required cookies These cookies are used to ensure the user has a secure journey through the site. earcusessionid - Used to maintain your session. earcusession - Used to secure your session. earcucc - Used to manage your cookie preferences. Analytics Cookies Analytics cookies or performance cookies are used to track website visitors and their user behaviour. _ga - Used by Google Analytics. _gid - Used by Google Analytics. _gat - Used by Google Analytics. _fbp - Used by Meta (Facebook) Pixel. Accept Cookies Accept All Cookies Customise Cookies Reject All Optional"
