    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/data-insight-officer-9042-manchester-all-saints-campus/8977/description/": {
      "title": "Data Insight Officer",
      "description": "Data Insight Officer - (9042) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Data Insight Officer (9042) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Data Insight Officer - (9042) Do you enjoy turning complex data into meaningful insight that drives decision-making and service improvement? Are you passionate about using data to make a real difference to the student experience? If so, this role could be for you! About the role: We have an exciting opportunity for a Data Insight Officer to join the Student Services Operations team on a full-time, two-year fixed-term basis. This is a key role within Student Services, supporting teams across a range of areas including student engagement; inclusion and disability; counselling, mental health and wellbeing; financial support; chaplaincy and pastoral support and study skills, as well as an extensive sport provision. Working closely with colleagues across the Directorate, you will help shape how data and insight are used to evaluate services, understand student needs and inform strategic decision-making. The post holder will design and develop of a new suite of Power BI dashboards and management reports, providing timely and actionable insight for service leaders. You will work with complex datasets from multiple systems, applying data modelling, data manipulation and analytical techniques to identify trends, evaluate impact and support evidence-based decision-making. A key focus of the role will be strengthening the Directorate's reporting infrastructure through the development of automated data processing and transformation workflows, using tools such as Power Query and Alteryx to improve efficiency, consistency and data quality. About you: We are looking for someone who combines strong technical expertise with excellent communication skills. You'll be confident translating complex information into clear and compelling insight, and building effective visual reporting solutions that support both operational and strategic priorities. The ideal candidate will have: Excellent analytical and data visualisation skills, with practical experience of Power BI, reporting and business intelligence tools. Experience of data manipulation and transformation, using tools such as Power Query, Alteryx or similar software. Strong communication and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to explain complex technical concepts to a range of audiences. A proactive approach to problem solving, identifying opportunities for improvement and supporting service development through data and insight. A little more about our team: You'll be joining the Student Services Operations team, which provides business process, systems, reporting and analytical support across the Student Services Directorate. Student Services delivers a wide range of support that enables students to thrive throughout their university career. The Directorate works across student engagement, inclusion and disability, counselling, mental health and wellbeing, financial support, chaplaincy and pastoral support, academic and study skills, and sport, ensuring students have access to the services and interventions they need to succeed. This role offers an excellent opportunity to help shape how data and insight are used across Student Services, working on reporting, systems and improvement projects that have a direct impact on services and student outcomes. You'll be supported to develop your expertise, build strong networks across the University and contribute to meaningful change. How to apply: To apply for this role, please submit the following: An up-to-date CV A covering letter (maximum two pages) detailing your suitability for the role and demonstrating how you meet the essential criteria: Specifically 1.1, 1.2, 1.3, 1.4, 2.1, 4.1 and 4.2 as set out in the Person Specification in the attached Job Description below. Responses to the two application questions , providing evidence of your experience in: (1) Developing reports, dashboards and data visualisations to support decision-making and, (2) Using data transformation and/or ETL tools to improve reporting efficiency or data quality. For an informal discussion about the role, please contact: Loren Dean-Austin, Senior Manager: Business Processes, Data and Reporting , l.dean-austin@mmu.ac.uk Please note: Interviews are provisionally scheduled to take place on 26 and 27 November 2026. Candidates are therefore encouraged to keep these dates available where possible as rescheduling may not be possible. Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy. This vacancy is expected to attract a high volume of applications. Therefore, under the Disability Confident Scheme, only disabled people who apply under the scheme and best meet the essential criteria will be offered an interview. Documents Candidate Pack.pdf (9.15 MB) Job Description - Data Insight Officer (Student Services).pdf (128.77 KB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: Academic Services Salary: Grade 7 £35,608 to £39,906) Closing Date: 4 November 2026 Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract Length: 2 year fixed term Contracted Hours per week: 35 Benefits 25 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays (Extra 5 days after 5 years of service) Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Hybrid working opportunities Meet the recruiter Claire Muir ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved. Cookie Preferences This site uses cookies and other tracking technologies to improve your browsing experience, show personalised content/ads and analyse site traffic. Select cookies to accept Required cookies These cookies are used to ensure the user has a secure journey through the site. earcusessionid - Used to maintain your session. earcusession - Used to secure your session. earcucc - Used to manage your cookie preferences. Analytics Cookies Analytics cookies or performance cookies are used to track website visitors and their user behaviour. _ga - Used by Google Analytics. _gid - Used by Google Analytics. _gat - Used by Google Analytics. _fbp - Used by Meta (Facebook) Pixel. Accept Cookies Accept All Cookies Customise Cookies Reject All Optional"
