    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/technical-specialist----ai--creative-technology-9418-manchester-all-saints-campus/9321/description/": {
      "title": "Technical Specialist",
      "description": "Technical Specialist -  AI & Creative Technology - (9418) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Technical Specialist -  AI & Creative Technology (9418) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Technical Specialist -  AI & Creative Technology - (9418) This role forms part of an exciting recruitment campaign within Technical Services, as we invest additional focus and resource into strengthening our capability across broadcast media technologies and the fast-evolving AI landscape. We are growing our Digital Arts team so that students and academics continue to benefit from industry-leading equipment, expertise and support as these fields advance at pace, and this is a great opportunity to help shape that development from the ground up. About our team: Technical Services are a large and diverse team of highly skilled technical professionals who ensure the optimal functioning of specialist spaces and resources to deliver an exceptional student experience. We work in specialist laboratories, workshops, studios, resource centres and IT facilities. Our technical professionals play a key role supporting, guiding, and advising students across our university from sciences, art, design and technology, through to sports, ceramics, nursing and physiotherapy. About the role and you: This role sits in the Digital Arts team, who provide specialist technical support to the School of Digital Arts (SODA) and the wider Arts & Humanities Faculty. As Technical Services lead for AI & Creative Technology (CreaTech), the post-holder will hold responsibility for the development, adoption and embedding of the specialism across education, research and knowledge exchange, working in collaboration with senior academic colleagues to shape its future direction. The ideal candidate will have demonstrable leadership ability and expertise spanning AI and software development at one end, and creative technology, human-AI interaction and design at the other. They will be experienced in: Python, PyTorch, TensorFlow and Hugging Face GPU/AI compute systems (NVIDIA GPUs, CUDA) AI-enabled creative production workflows (ComfyUI, Stable Diffusion) interaction and AI design/prototyping tools (Figma, Adobe XD) planning and managing work across a specialism, including matrix management of others They will lead the strategic direction of the specialism, plan and manage work across both disciplines, and support students and academics in developing industry-standard AI and creative technology skills. Experience of leading AI or CreaTech projects and setting strategic direction would be advantageous, as well as the ability to demonstrate and instruct to a high standard. The role will involve supporting staff and students on a diverse number of customer-facing specialist counters and support areas. The successful candidate will have a proven track record of accomplishment in a similar environment. Additionally, they will have a positive and flexible approach to work, be reliable and punctual as well as motivated and willing to undertake all required training and allocated tasks. They will have the ability to work alongside others and be capable of working in a team, whilst striving to deliver excellent customer service. Strong communication and interpersonal skills are key as well as being able to demonstrate ownership of personal workload. At Manchester Metropolitan University, we are committed to supporting our technical staff in enabling them to undertake development activities in line with the needs of their specialism and work area, so a willingness to learn and develop is essential. If you are enthusiastic about this area, flexible, and committed to providing a high level of customer service, we would love to hear from you. How to apply: To apply for this vacancy please submit a covering letter (no more than one-page A4) and a CV (no more than two pages A4), addressing how you meet the essential criteria of the post via our online portal. Click \"Apply Now\" to submit your application. Please note that applications must be submitted through the online portal, applications received by email will not be considered. If you would like more information about this vacancy, please contact Leighton Moody, Technical Services Manager. Email: L.Moody@mmu.ac.uk Interviews are provisionally scheduled for 26 November (26/11/2026). Candidates should make every effort to be available on these dates, as alternative interview dates may not be possible. Please note: Applications received during the previous recruitment campaign have already been fully considered and, therefore, previous applicants need not re-apply, as repeat applications will not be considered. Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy. Documents Candidate Pack.pdf (9.16 MB) Technical Specialist - AI & Creative Technology (CreaTech).pdf (79.38 KB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: Academic Services Salary: Grade 7 (£35,608 to £39,906) Closing Date: 10 November 2026 Contract Type: Permanent Contracted Hours per week: 35 Benefits 25 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays (Extra 5 days after 5 years of service) Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Meet the recruiter Claire Muir ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved."
    },
    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/edi-project-officer-9676-manchester-all-saints-campus/9572/description/": {
      "title": "EDI Project Officer",
      "description": "EDI Project Officer - (9676) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - EDI Project Officer (9676) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login EDI Project Officer - (9676) Equality, Diversity and Inclusion (EDI) Project Officer Why join us? Become part of our collaborative culture, diverse teams and well-connected community. At Manchester Met, we're committed to creating a workplace where everyone can thrive. As our Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Project Officer, you'll play a vital role in delivering initiatives that strengthen belonging, celebrate diversity and support our ambition to be a truly inclusive university. Every project you support will help shape the experience of more than 5,000 colleagues and contribute to our commitment to Transforming Lives Together. What you'll do Working within the Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Team, you'll provide high-quality project and administrative support across a varied portfolio of EDI programmes and initiatives. Reporting to the Head of Equality, Diversity and Inclusion, you'll help bring our Equality Objectives to life through effective coordination, stakeholder engagement and project delivery. Key responsibilities include: Supporting the delivery of strategic EDI projects and programmes across the University. Developing and maintaining project plans, tracking milestones and monitoring progress. Coordinating meetings, events, staff network activities and engagement initiatives. Diary management for the Director of Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Supporting communications activity through digital channels, intranet content and internal campaigns. Managing team administration, including diary management, procurement processes, event coordination and stakeholder communications. Gathering feedback, analysing data and preparing reports that help inform future activity. Building effective relationships with colleagues and external partners to support collaborative delivery of EDI priorities. This is an exciting opportunity to contribute to work that makes a tangible difference, helping to foster a culture where every colleague feels valued, respected and able to reach their full potential. Who we're looking for You will be a highly organised and proactive professional who enjoys coordinating multiple priorities and building positive relationships with a wide range of stakeholders. You'll bring: Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Strong organisational and planning abilities. Experience using Microsoft 365 and managing varied administrative activities. The ability to work independently while supporting multiple projects and deadlines. Strong relationship-building and stakeholder engagement skills. An interest in, and commitment to, equality, diversity and inclusion. A positive, solutions-focused approach and the confidence to adapt in a fast-paced environment. A degree or equivalent qualification, or substantial relevant experience, is essential. Experience of project coordination and communicating with diverse stakeholder groups will help you succeed in this role. What you'll receive At Manchester Met, you'll join a diverse and inclusive community that values your contribution and supports your development. You'll benefit from: A supportive, people-led culture. Professional and career development opportunities. Flexible and hybrid working arrangements where appropriate. Generous annual leave entitlement plus University closure days. An excellent pension scheme. Health, wellbeing and employee support services. Staff networks, communities and opportunities to get involved across the University. The opportunity to work in a University recognised for its commitment to equality, diversity and inclusion. Be part of something bigger At Manchester Met, we're proudly driving progress through education, research and social impact. We're a diverse and connected community where every voice matters and where colleagues are empowered to make meaningful contributions. If you're passionate about equality, diversity and inclusion and want to help create positive change, we'd love to hear from you. Choose an impactful role and become a valued member of our welcoming and inclusive community. Join us as we continue transforming lives together. Apply today. How to apply Please submit a CV and a Cover Letter (maximum 2 pages) that clearly demonstrates how you meet the essential and desirable criteria outlined in the attached Job Description. Use your cover letter to provide specific examples of your skills and experience relevant to the role – Please note, applications without a cover letter may not be considered at shortlisting stage. Closing date: 13 th November 2026 Interview Dates: 24 th and 25 th November We would encourage candidates to make note of these dates in the event that you are successfully shortlisted. Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy. For any informal enquiries about the role, please contact, Amraze Khan, Head of EDI on Amraze.Khan@mmu.ac.uk #LI-MP1 Documents Equality, Diversity, and Inclusion Project Officer - UPDATED JUL2024.pdf (273.08 KB) Professional Services Candidate Pack.pdf (9.15 MB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: People & Organisational Development Salary: Grade 5 (££28,592 - £30,986) Closing Date: 13 November 2026 Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract Length: 12 months Contracted Hours per week: 35 hours per week Benefits 25 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays (Extra 5 days after 5 years of service) Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Meet the recruiter Michael Platt ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved. Cookie Preferences This site uses cookies and other tracking technologies to improve your browsing experience, show personalised content/ads and analyse site traffic. Select cookies to accept Required cookies These cookies are used to ensure the user has a secure journey through the site. earcusessionid - Used to maintain your session. earcusession - Used to secure your session. earcucc - Used to manage your cookie preferences. Analytics Cookies Analytics cookies or performance cookies are used to track website visitors and their user behaviour. _ga - Used by Google Analytics. _gid - Used by Google Analytics. _gat - Used by Google Analytics. _fbp - Used by Meta (Facebook) Pixel. Accept Cookies Accept All Cookies Customise Cookies Reject All Optional"
    }
